        "raw": "<p>3) why are we taking for granted that seeds played from the environment deck enter Akash&rsquo;thriya play zone and don&rsquo;t stay in the environment play zone instead?</p><p>Unity&rsquo;s golems played from Guise deck or Shinobi Assassins are not good examples because primordial seeds cards are part of Akash&rsquo;thriya mechanic and are designed to be played from the environment deck. Moreover in an Oblivaeon&rsquo;s game, how come a card played from Guise deck enter Unity&rsquo;s play area if they are in two different battle zones and we have to treat each battle zone as its own Sentinels match, where the other battle zone is completely non-existing?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Having those cards instantly move to their original deck&rsquo;s play area raises more questions than it answers.&nbsp;</p>",
